WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.610
- The Saw franchise is known

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:03.900
for the 21st century
mechanical torture devices

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.040
devised by its antagonist, John Kramer,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.430
also known as Jigsaw.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.470
The traps have become as
important to a Saw movie

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.090
as the gadgets are to
007, or I don't know,

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.860
like the dinosaurs to Jurassic Park.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.380
In fact, the series has gained
a little bit of a reputation

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.820
for its masochistic tendencies.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.340
In honor of there being
a new Saw movie out,

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.700
I've teamed up with fellow
masochist, I mean, Saw fan,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.190
Sarah Hawkinson, also known
as Possessed by Horror,

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.630
to talk about our five favorite Saw traps.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.130
We also ranked the Saw movies,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.580
so stick around to the end of this video

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.837
to see how everything stacks up.

00:00:33.837 --> 00:00:36.420
(upbeat music)

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.720
- For my criteria, how I
chose my top five Saw traps,

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.700
is number one, survivability.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.090
It has to be survivable.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.330
Any fake-out traps where
they actually complete it,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.130
but still die, not
gonna choose from those.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.580
Number two, plausibility.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.250
It has to seem realistic,

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.850
both physics wise and human body wise.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.480
Can you really die like that?

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.330
Can you die that quickly from that?

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.330
And finally, number three,

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.670
originality and creativity, of course.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.130
I feel like some traps
just aren't that creative

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.880
or they're used repeatedly,
like the reverse bear trap,

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.410
or they're just too similar
to previous traps used,

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.870
so I want all original,

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.760
I would never have thought about that.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.370
Okay, starting with my fifth
favorite Saw trap of all time,

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:24.840
we have Jeff's trial,
specifically the freezer room,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.270
from Saw III.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.450
This technically isn't a trap
of the woman in the trap.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.790
It is, of course, relying
on Jeff's decision.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:37.000
And it is technically a
test for Jeff himself.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.220
And there's a lot of traps like this

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.210
where it kind of relies on
other people or another person.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.530
And these typically aren't my favorite

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.030
because they do seem a little bit

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.990
out of the person's control.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.720
In this trap, Jeff must
face the only witness

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.670
that saw the hit and run
accident that killed his son.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.170
And of course, he must decide
if he will choose to save her.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.470
The technicality of this trap,

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.740
he must reach behind cooling pipes

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.230
in order to retrieve a key
that will unlock the lock

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.730
that is holding her up.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.820
And this requires him to
push his face onto the pipes,

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.860
ultimately ripping flesh off.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.450
And he has a limited time to do this

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.900
because, of course, in the freezer room,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.150
she is strung up naked and
water is being blasted onto her

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:21.090
and kind of creating a Popsicle effect.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.950
Of course, this is one
of my favorite Saw traps.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.350
It's been one of my favorite traps

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.580
pretty much ever since I saw Saw III.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.030
However, it's fifth on this list

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:29.110
because although technically,

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.340
he had a chance to save the woman,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.520
he still needed that key
to enter the next room.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.000
The only iffy criteria

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.060
that this kind of doesn't
really meet is the plausibility.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.960
We don't know how long
she was hanging there

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.770
before Jeff entered the room.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:44.970
And I don't know if she'd necessarily

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.820
become a human Popsicle that quickly.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.850
Maybe time had passed, I don't know.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.683
We don't know.

00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:52.010
We also don't know how cold the room is.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.330
Maybe it's really, really cold

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.551
and she would become a Popsicle.

00:02:54.551 --> 00:02:55.540
We don't know.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.330
But that's the only thing that
I could fault this trap for

00:02:58.330 --> 00:02:59.968
is a little bit of the plausibility.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.700
- [Jigsaw] Can you find it
within you to save another?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.260
- I came up with five factors
to judge the traps on.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.400
Is it fair and winnable?

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.650
Could it effectively
transform a bad person?

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.240
Does the punishment fit the crime?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.150
Does it look cool?

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.510
And is it brutal?

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.770
My honorable mention is gonna go

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.660
to the neck tie trap from Saw V.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.080
I like that there's a puzzle element

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.380
that the characters have to figure out,

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.250
and I also like that
there's a social aspect,

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.660
but it doesn't really do that well

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.960
in any of my five factors,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.850
so I'm gonna have to count that one out.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.770
My number five is going to be
the angel trap from Saw III.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.080
In this trap, Detective
Allison Kerry is tested

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.140
because Jigsaw believes that
she spends too much time

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.050
piecing together the
final moments of the dead

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.930
and that this has made
her dead on the inside.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.130
This near-death experience

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.030
is supposed to make her
appreciate life again.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.810
The device is hooked into her ribcage

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.090
and the only way she can
escape is by retrieving the key

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.740
from inside of a vat of acid.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.780
And she has just 60 seconds to do so.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.330
Once time expires, the
brackets pull her ribcage apart

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.510
if she's unable to unhook
herself from the device.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.620
This is a trap that
should be fair on paper,

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.950
only the apprentice
responsible for setting it up,

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.070
Amanda, rigged it by putting the wrong key

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.660
in the vat of acid because she felt

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.370
that Detective Kerry deserved to die.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.080
Kerry doesn't really deserve to be tested

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:03.913
in the first place.

00:04:03.913 --> 00:04:06.230
She's only targeted because
she's investigating Jigsaw.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.670
But if someone had lost
their appreciation for life,

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.150
I could see the angel trap
being a wake-up call for them.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.250
Does it look cool?

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.083
Yes.

00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:15.080
Visually, this is
probably my favorite trap.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.260
I love the distorted view
we see of Allison's face

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.240
through the acid beaker

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.610
and there's just something beautiful

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.910
about the symmetry of the room,

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.490
the way the colored light falls on her,

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.150
and the pose that the machine puts her in

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.420
certainly lives up to
the angelic namesake.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.740
This is one of the more
brutal traps in the series,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.180
based on an ancient torture device

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.260
from Norse mythology
called the Blood Eagle.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.980
We actually see it go off on camera.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.430
They don't get fancy and try to hide it

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.650
with camera angles and editing.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.693
She just gets destroyed by
this thing, and it is messy.

00:04:44.111 --> 00:04:45.150
- You.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.230
- All right, in fourth
place is pound of flesh.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.400
The two in this trap are Eddie and Simone,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.720
who are money lenders
who lent too much money

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.440
to people who could not pay it back,

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.800
and thus, entered inescapable debt.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.490
The technicalities of this test

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.600
are whoever gives the most amount of flesh

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.530
within 60 seconds survives
and they are fighting

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.740
against the clock because
during that 60 seconds,

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:09.130
screws are being screwed into
the sides of their skull.

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:11.830
I like this test a lot because
it doesn't say specifically

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.810
how much flesh you have to sacrifice.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.070
It's just whoever sacrifices the most,

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.070
and size doesn't necessarily matter.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:22.880
Obviously, Eddie is a bigger
dude and Simone recognizes this

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.400
and realizes that she's gonna
have to cut off much more

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.120
than just fleshy bits in order to win.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.953
What does she do?

00:05:29.953 --> 00:05:33.480
Sacrifices entire limbs with bones.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.170
An interesting fact about pound of flesh

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.140
is that this is actually a reference

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.410
to Shakespeare's Merchant of Venice.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:42.300
This refers to a money lender
who lends money to his rival

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.610
and making the security
for the transaction

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.740
a pound of flesh if it
cannot be paid back.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.160
When the rival defaults on the loan,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.910
the money lender demands the
pound of flesh in return.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.680
Another one of my biases
towards this trap,

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.520
and one of the reasons
why it's in my top five,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.070
is because Simone is
played by Tanedra Howard,

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.980
who actually won a reality
competition show for this role.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.689
She was in a show called Scream Queens.

00:06:02.689 --> 00:06:05.833
- [Narrator] From Lionsgate
and Twisted Pictures,

00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:08.033
a breakout role and the next big star

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:12.490
in horror's biggest franchise, Saw.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.320
- Saw will save us.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.500
- And Shawnee Smith, who plays
Amanda in the Saw franchise,

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.340
is actually the host of this show.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.360
I just really like the
connection, and Tanedra,

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.350
I feel like, does such an amazing job

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.540
and was so well-deserved at this role.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.220
- You want to know the best
thing that happened to me

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.403
after having to cut off my own arm?

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:36.140
It's handicapped parking at the damn mall.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:36.973
- Number four.

00:06:36.973 --> 00:06:38.810
I'm going more recent for my next trap.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.990
Now, when I first saw the
subway trap in Spiral,

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.800
I felt like it was
something I'd seen before,

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.400
but after thinking about it,
it's actually pretty original.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.340
The subject is Detective Mark Boswick,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.640
who was tested because he gave
false testimonies in court

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.880
to get people thrown in jail.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.020
His tongue is clamped to
a metal device overhead

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.040
and he's standing on a ladder

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.360
in the middle of a subway tunnel.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.930
His objective was to
get off of the ladder,

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.110
and thus ripping out the
tongue that was responsible

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:00.600
for all of those damaging lies.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.890
And he had until the next
train came through to do so.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.410
In this sense, the punishment
really does fit the crime.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.320
We've seen a victim get tested by Jigsaw

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.810
for the things they have said in the past.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.720
For example, Nina in Saw seven.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.500
But this is surprisingly the first time

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.720
a killer has literally gone
after the victim's tongue,

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:15.840
though I have seen it before

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.545
in another James Wan
property, Dead Silence.

00:07:18.545 --> 00:07:21.128
(creepy music)

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.720
This trap really doesn't look that cool,

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.660
but it is winnable, assuming it's possible

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.830
to survive something like that.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.443
And regardless of the
outcome, it's very brutal.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.940
(intense tones)

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.040
- Next up, I wanted to
rank this one higher,

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.940
I'm not gonna lie, just
because of what it is

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:43.710
and how intense it is, the
scalping seat from Saw IV.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.280
Now, this is another layered joint test

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.520
with Detective Rigg being tested

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.490
while the victim of the trap, Brenda,

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.060
is also going through her own test.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.190
The two tests are Detective Rigg is told

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.020
not to attempt to save the victim

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.010
because that is always in his instincts

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.420
and that he is obsessed with
saving everyone around him.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.180
This time, he must fight his instincts

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.270
and allow Brenda to suffer the trap.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.030
I don't wanna say die
because I really don't know

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.010
if scalping would really kill you,

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.990
which we'll get to plausibility
in a minute. (chuckles)

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.790
Brenda, who is a criminal
pimp forcing young women

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:17.820
to prostitute for her,
is attached to a machine,

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:19.700
which is attached to her hair,

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:23.300
which slowly is pulling
her hair off, scalping her.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:26.220
And as the mechanism turns, a
code is revealed on the back

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.750
and Rigg decides to help
her before it's too late.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.830
Around the room were evidence photos

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.290
of Brenda that could incriminate her,

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:36.290
so her test was, if a
cop comes to save you,

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.120
you must kill him before
he can arrest you.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.290
Thus, it is in Detective
Rigg's best interest

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:44.190
not to help the victim for
the first time in his life.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.660
It's a little bit complicated
layer tests going on here.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:51.100
There's very few traps, I
would say, in the Saw universe

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.610
that have this layered effect.

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:55.170
Obviously, there's joint traps,
there's competitive traps,

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:58.530
there's reliant traps,
there's group traps,

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.280
but very few layer joint traps. (chuckles)

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.640
Although I don't
technically believe, I mean,

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.850
maybe you could die from being scalped.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.866
The head does bleed a lot.

00:09:07.866 --> 00:09:10.300
Plausibility is a little iffy on this one,

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.880
but I chose it as one of my favorites

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.190
and in third place specifically

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:17.467
because it is just one of the
most intense traps to watch.

00:09:17.467 --> 00:09:21.017
- (screaming) They're in the gears

00:09:21.017 --> 00:09:21.896
- What's in the gears?

00:09:21.896 --> 00:09:22.962
- The combination.

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:24.085
Get me out!

00:09:24.085 --> 00:09:26.752
(intense tones)

00:09:28.155 --> 00:09:29.730
(upbeat music)

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:30.570
- Number three.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:33.020
For my number three I'm
taking it back, once again,

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.980
to Saw III, which contains
one of the most unique traps

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:37.560
in the series, the pig vat.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:38.890
This trap features Jeff Denlon,

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.550
who can't stop mourning for his dead son

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.660
and fantasizing about
revenge on his killer.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.870
While most Saw traps attempt
to transform a victim

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:45.920
through physical suffering,

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.500
the pig vat deals in more
of an emotional suffering.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.540
Jeff is forced to burn his
child's old possessions

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.830
in order to obtain a key with
the power to free the judge

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.300
who let the killer go off easy.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.200
If Jeff is unable to do so in time,

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.090
the judge will be drowned in pig guts.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.400
This is one of those rare
cases where the test subjects

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.560
all survive, but it isn't without
a major internal struggle.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:05.480
It's also effective because
the goal is for Jeff

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.490
to let go of his past.

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:08.720
And he literally has to
do so in order to win.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:10.920
For Jeff, the punishment
definitely fits the crime,

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.800
but for the judge, not really.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.560
He just made a mistake and he
nearly loses his life over it.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.380
Now, maybe some people will disagree,

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.180
but I really love the look of this trap,

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.830
particularly because we get
to see the maggot-covered pigs

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.410
get brought out in a factory line

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.330
and dropped into a shredder and liquified

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.570
as they fall into the vat.

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:28.890
I love the way the sound
design makes this even scarier.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:31.690
And of course, the metal
soundtrack adds to the intensity.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.320
When it comes to the-
- Brutality!

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.500
- I'm kind of split here.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.360
It's not really that
brutal for Jeff at all

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.770
because he's only experiencing
an emotional pain,

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.960
but for the judge, I'd
say it's pretty rough.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:43.610
Not only is he nearly drowned,
but just imagine the smell

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:45.830
and taste of getting
buried alive in pig guts.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.110
I'd take the corn silo over that any day.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.010
- [Jigsaw] Your soul will never recover.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:51.730
Now, you have the power

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:55.240
to sentence his soul straight to hell.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:56.170
- In second place,

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:59.600
we have the infamous
needle pit from Saw II.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.440
I think this trap is so famous,

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.770
and a lot of people probably
think about this trap

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:05.830
when they think about the Saw franchise.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:08.990
Now, the test is actually
for Xavier, but as we know,

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:11.870
Amanda is the one who ends up in the pit.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:14.400
Xavier picks up Amanda,
throws her in the pit,

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.150
which just adds to the intensity.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.930
It's not like someone
willingly jumped in there.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:22.530
She is thrown unwillingly
into the pit of needles.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.400
And of course, among the needles is a key

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.040
that opens a door where
there is an antidote

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.350
for the nerve gas that
is slowly being released

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.650
in the house that they're
in, trapped in, I should say.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.750
I think this is one of the most
ultimate uncomfortable traps

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.560
to watch, one of the
most intense to watch.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:37.900
I cringe every single time,

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.740
even though I've seen it a million times.

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:41.720
Of course, we know if you
don't reach the antidote,

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.130
you could die from the nerve gas

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.130
being pumped into the house.

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:46.900
And of course, there
are many smaller traps

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:48.170
throughout the house that lead

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:50.270
to the antidote to this nerve gas.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:52.820
Fun fact about this trap
is in order to film it,

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.460
they had to remove every single needle

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.910
from every single syringe

00:11:56.910 --> 00:12:00.350
and replace it with a fiber
needle, which took several days,

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:04.453
and they had to use over 120,000 syringes.

00:12:05.307 --> 00:12:08.120
- [Jigsaw] It will be like
finding a needle in a haystack.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:08.970
- Number two.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.420
The subject of our next
trap, like Jeff Denlon,

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:13.550
is faced with more of
a psychological torture

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:14.520
than a physical one.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.870
His name is William Easton,

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.290
and he's a health insurance executive

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.060
for a company called Umbrella Health.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.180
William was responsible
for creating the algorithm

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.320
to determine who the lowest
risk individuals are.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.350
If he determines that
they're unlikely to get sick,

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:26.580
he'll offer them coverage.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:29.730
Jigsaw sees this as William
deciding who lives and who dies

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:31.740
and decides to give him a
taste of his own medicine

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:33.520
in a trap called the gallows.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.570
William is persuaded to
take hold of two chains.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.366
And after a very Dark Knight
appearance of Billy the Puppet,

00:12:38.366 --> 00:12:39.390
(intense tones)

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.890
is presented with two people
on barbed wire nooses.

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:44.070
One is his secretary, an older woman

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.640
with a history of diabetes
and a loving family.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.050
The other is his file
clerk, a young healthy man

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:51.200
with no living relatives
to mourn his loss.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.720
According to William's algorithm,

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.490
the secretary should be denied coverage

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:56.130
and the file clerk should be treated.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.530
But when presented with a
choice between two colleagues

00:12:58.530 --> 00:12:59.410
he knows personally,

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.520
the choice is not quite as easy to make.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:03.530
The trap takes place in a reptile habitat.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:05.210
It's symbolic of the cold-blooded nature

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:06.330
of William's decisions.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:08.090
Is this trap fair or winnable?

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.660
That's one of my gripes with it.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.170
Someone has to die here.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.820
You could argue that
they're all wrongdoers

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:14.440
for working at a dirty insurance company,

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.840
but it's not very fair to
the people wearing the nooses

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.390
who are really just
trying to make a living.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.510
Aside from that, I would
anticipate that being faced

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:22.090
with a traumatizing decision like this

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:22.923
would have caused William

00:13:22.923 --> 00:13:25.140
to reconsider his policies
at the very least.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:26.570
Visually, it's nothing special.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:27.950
It's just two people standing there.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.050
And while it's probably
a painful way to die,

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:32.170
it's a lot quicker than
a lot of the other traps

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.900
that put a victim through
extended periods of suffering.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.770
It's really just John
Kramer's creative method

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:37.720
of turning the tables

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.880
that makes the gallows
such a memorable trap.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:43.150
- [Jigsaw] As you can see,
the choice is not so clear

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.910
when you are face to face with the people

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.300
whose blood will stain your hands.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.270
- All right, now for my
favorite, favorite Saw trap

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.280
of all time, the spike trap,

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:56.400
otherwise known as Cupid's
arrows, from Saw IV.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.680
And I feel like this one is a
controversial one to put first

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.920
because there are many,
many more iconic Saw traps,

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.440
but I just feel so drawn to this one.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.320
And like I said in my video

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.510
where we rank all the Saw movies,

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:13.210
Saw IV has objectively some of
the best traps in my opinion.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.390
This trap involves Morgan and
Rex, who are a married couple,

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.630
and they wake up to realize
that they are attached

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.060
by arrows or spikes.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.700
And the test is that Morgan
finally has the opportunity

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:27.630
to break the ties that bind
her to her abusive husband.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:31.380
The catch is in this, is
as she removes each spike

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:34.950
or each arrow from her
body, pulls it through,

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:38.830
it will slowly make her husband bleed out.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:41.550
She is in-penetrated, is that a word,

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:43.640
through many, many points of her body.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.570
However, none of them lethal.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.930
Whereas, her husband is
punctured through major arteries.

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:52.160
I just feel like this is
such a strong scene to me

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:55.500
because of the emotions
attached to this couple,

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.060
even though we hardly know them.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.590
It's just something
that I feel so drawn to

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:01.751
and to watch the intensity

00:15:01.751 --> 00:15:05.140
and the strength and the independence.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:07.210
I know this is way too
deep for just a Saw trap,

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.110
but just go with it for a second.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:12.150
She's finally choosing to
break ties with her husband.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:15.170
Is it really just her
survival instinct kicking in?

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:18.191
Probably, but she didn't
really have that going for her

00:15:18.191 --> 00:15:20.780
when she was with her abusive husband.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:23.030
And he's pulling on the
spikes trying to prevent her

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.410
from pulling it out, and it's
just a very, very intense

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.010
and heartbreaking scene in a way.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:32.210
It's just, it's my favorite
scene or favorite trap by far.

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.960
Also, I love the concept of this.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:38.700
This has to be the most
original Saw trap in my opinion.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.831
And I just love it.

00:15:40.831 --> 00:15:43.840
- [Jigsaw] The human body
is a fascinating organism.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.490
- This probably comes as no surprise.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.700
One of the most iconic, cringe-inducing,

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:49.230
and well-balanced traps in the history

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:51.370
of the Saw franchise comes in Saw II,

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.170
and it's called the needle pit.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.620
Amanda is forced to rummage
through piles of syringes,

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.530
causing many of them
to stick into her flesh

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:59.150
as she relives her days as an addict

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:00.950
while desperately
searching for her antidote.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.670
We don't know what was in the syringes,

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:05.390
but the assumption is that
it's something pretty nasty.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:06.680
Ultimately, she finds the key,

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.440
but Xavier is slightly too late

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.670
when it comes to opening the safe

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.610
and the whole thing ends up being a loss.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.390
The challenge is actually very doable.

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:14.940
You would just need to
have a lot of willpower

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.230
to keep pushing through the pile

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.470
as more and more needles
pin themselves into you.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.220
But theoretically, once
you get the antidote,

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:21.460
you'd be able to survive.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:24.040
Could the needle pit effectively
transform its subjects?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.430
We don't actually see the answer

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.610
because the intended subject
never goes through the trap,

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.430
but I think it's somewhat questionable.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.870
Xavier probably already
knew that drugs are bad

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:34.150
before he became a dealer,
and I'm not really sure

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:36.080
that being in their shoes for two minutes

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.260
would cause him to reconsider
his career options.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.760
At the very least, it might've
made a less evil character

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:43.050
realize how much drugs can
mess up a person's life,

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:45.410
but it seems unlikely that
it would have any effect.

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.180
This trap takes place
inside of what appears

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.840
to be a nursery inside the house.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:50.070
When a junkie becomes addicted,

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.080
their bodies become
dependent on the drugs.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.150
Just as a baby needs its
parents to provide for it,

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.720
the drug addicts need
to keep crawling back

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:57.270
to Xavier to get their fix.

00:16:57.270 --> 00:17:00.010
I can say the punishment probably
fits the crime on this one

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.520
because the amount of needles in the pit

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.430
is probably comparable
to the amount of drugs

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.330
that Xavier has sold in his lifetime.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.900
Jigsaw is essentially forcing him

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.410
to go through all of it at once.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:10.450
Does this trap look cool?

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:11.970
It definitely looks ugly,

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:14.090
but I have to give this
one some creativity points

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.960
for not just being a big hunk of machinery

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.820
like so many other Saw traps are.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.920
The yellow lighting in
this room is disgusting,

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.410
but I think it accomplishes its goal

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:22.890
to make us feel uncomfortable.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.020
The way the needles stick
to her is really well done.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.220
And I know it makes a
lot of Saw fans cringe.

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:28.730
In fact, I know there are a lot of people

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.170
who can't even do a single needle,

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:33.600
so this trap is truly a
trypanophobic's worst nightmare.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.280
Where does this land on the pain scale?

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.830
Probably not super high.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:37.663
At the end of the day,

00:17:37.663 --> 00:17:39.170
you're just getting
poked all over your body.

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:40.860
You're not getting
flesh ripped out of you,

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:42.530
you're not getting burned or drowned,

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:43.910
but I'm still gonna make a case for this

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.800
being one of the most unforgiving traps

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.480
because this is one of those Jigsaw traps

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.030
that forces the participant
to harm themselves.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:52.450
Many of the other traps are
out of the player's hands,

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:54.080
whatever happens to them happens.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.170
The thing with the needle pits,

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.860
and a few other traps in the series,

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:59.080
is that you have to put
yourself in pain to succeed,

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.040
which goes against what
your brain wants you to do.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.430
You can see in her reaction

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.540
how getting stabbed in
dozens of places like that

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.260
really causes the pain to stack up.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.340
And for Amanda specifically,
it's much harder

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:10.660
because she has already
overcome the life of drugs.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.970
She thought it was over, but
now she's finding herself

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:15.640
being thrown back in
with no shoes at that.

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:17.130
Now a lot of you have been asking,

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:18.890
what did I think of Spiral?

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.970
Where does it stack up
with the other Saw movies?

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:23.420
Sarah and I have created a second video

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:25.720
where we rank every
installment in the franchise.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:27.960
If you enjoy my content and
the topics I talk about,

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.680
you'll probably wanna
go ahead and subscribe

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:30.710
to Possessed by Horror.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.100
I originally found her channel
and started talking to her

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.030
because I found that her
reviews tended to line up

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:36.900
with my own horror movie taste.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.470
She's become one of the few
critics that I actually trust.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.710
You'll find our video on
the left, but before you go,

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:43.480
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:44.860
for new horrors every week,

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.910
ring the death bell for all notifications,

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:48.960
and I'll see you over in that other video,

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.900
assuming we both survive.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.640
I guess if Sarah survives also.

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:55.453
I mean, we already made the
video, so I think we're good.

